{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'cat /home/gw/.agents/skills/security-audit/SKILL.md'","aggregated_output":"---\nname: security-audit\ndescription: \"Run the repo's whole-surface security audit — 9-dimension fan-out, adversarially verified, reconciled against the findings ledger.\"\n---\n\n<!-- generated-by: link-codex-config.ts; source: gridwork-core -->\n\n## Identity\n\nThe engine-neutral whole-surface security sweep. The active orchestrator performs the fan-out\ndirectly, validates schema-shaped results, adversarially refutes high-impact candidates, and\nreconciles survivors through the repo audit CLI. It is the periodic WHOLE-surface sweep, not the\ndiff-scoped `gw-ship` review.\n\n## When to invoke / use\n\n- A whole-surface security pass is wanted (pre-launch, periodic, post-large-merge) — not a diff review.\n- You want findings tracked to closure across runs (new / regressed / closed), not re-listed.\n- The repo carries the audit harness (`audit/cli.ts` and `audit/findings.toml`).\n\n## When not to invoke / use\n\n- Reviewing a single in-flight diff — that is `gw-ship`'s SECURITY audit / `gw-security-auditor` directly.\n- A non-harness repo (no `audit/cli.ts`) — there is nothing to reconcile against.\n- Remediation — this produces the queue; fixing each finding is a separate phase per finding-batch.\n\n## Rules\n\n1. Parse `scope` (default `whole-app`) and `depth` (`quick|standard|exhaustive`, default `standard`).\n   Preflight `audit/cli.ts` + `audit/findings.toml`; if either is absent, stop before writing.\n2. Pack the `scope` subtree once with `repomix` per `feeding-context-with-repomix`\n   (one pack per lane/dimension subtree, at fan-out start). Pass the pack path in `args` so each of the 9\n   dimension agents' briefing carries it, instead of each dimension independently Grep/Read-ing the same\n   subtree. The audit is read-only — all 9 dimensions share this one initial pack; re-pack only between\n   iterations (feeding-context-with-repomix rule 7), never mid-sweep.\n3. Apply the depth contract: `quick` = one pass over authorization, secrets, money, input/SSRF,\n   and append-only integrity; `standard` = one pass over all nine dimensions; `exhaustive` = two\n   finder rounds over all dimensions plus three independent refuter votes per critical/high.\n4. Dispatch one `gw-security-auditor` per selected dimension in parallel, always backgrounded and\n   with an explicit security model (`fable` on Claude; generated `gw_security_auditor` at GPT\n   high reasoning on Codex). Every prompt includes the pack path, project AGENTS/CLAUDE rules,\n   `identity/security.md`, and exactly one dimension:\n   authorization · tenant/data isolation and RLS · sensitive-data handling · secrets and token\n   comparison · money/billing integrity · input validation and SSRF · headers/session/rate-limit\n   controls · append-only/WORM integrity · external egress.\n5. Require JSON shaped as `{ dimension, summary, findings[] }`; each finding requires\n   `severity,title,file,line,detail,fix`. Deduplicate by `file:line:title`. On exhaustive round two,\n   request only new edge/second-order findings and stop a dimension when it returns dry.\n6. For every critical/high candidate, dispatch independent `gw-security-auditor` refuters with\n   the same explicit model. Require `{ isReal,severity,confidence,reasoning }`; retain only a strict\n   majority of real votes. Medium/low findings pass through with medium confidence.\n7. Normalize survivors to the audit schema (`workflow=security`, `surface=security:<dimension>`),\n   write them to a temp JSON outside the repo, then run:\n   `bun audit/cli.ts reconcile --workflow security --in <tmp.json> --scope <scope> --depth <depth>`.\n8. Report the ledger delta (new / regressed / closed / unchanged), missing/null lanes, stats, and the dated report path\n   (`audit/reports/<date>-security.md`). Do NOT auto-fix; the report's remediation queue is the handoff.\n9. Never remediate or commit from this skill. `exhaustive` is a deliberate spend; name it.\n\n## Inputs\n\n`scope` + `depth` (optional; defaulted). The repo must contain the audit harness.\n\n## Outputs\n\nA dated `audit/reports/<date>-security.md` (severity-ranked findings + remediation queue + ledger\ndelta), an updated `audit/findings.toml`, and an inline summary of the delta.\n\n## Failure modes\n\n- `audit/cli.ts` missing → not a harness repo; stop and say so.\n- All completed lanes return zero findings → report \"clean vs the 9 dimensions at this depth\"; still reconcile to close stale ledger rows.\n- A dimension agent errors mid-fan-out → retain a null lane and name the coverage gap; never call the audit clean.\n\n## Examples\n\n**Bad:** invoking on an unmerged feature diff — use `gw-ship` SECURITY instead; this sweep is whole-surface.\n\n**Good:** `/security-audit scope:whole-app depth:standard` → 9 dimensions fan out, criticals/highs\nget a refuter, survivors reconcile against the ledger, report names 2 new + 1 regressed + 3 closed.\n\n## Why\n\nA security regression is the highest-cost agent-written failure. A saved, parameterized,\nledger-tracked whole-surface sweep makes \"re-run the security audit\" one command with continuity —\nthe swarm pattern formalized, not re-authored per audit.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
