{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'nl -ba .github/workflows/release-train.yml'","aggregated_output":"     1\tname: release-train\n     2\t# The ADR-0318 release train (R1–R4), reworked commit-addressable by ADR-0325. Publishing a\n     3\t# GitHub Release is THE trigger (R1) — its tag MUST target the merged version-PR commit\n     4\t# (version-pr.yml authored it; push-to-main CI proved it green). Everything rides it (R2):\n     5\t# registry tarball publish → registry Worker deploy → public-mirror sync → mirror npm publish →\n     6\t# site redeploy, in that order, each leg a dispatch of the existing workflow that already owns the\n     7\t# capability (no duplicated publish logic). Legs 1, 1b and 2 receive the release tag so they act on\n     8\t# EXACTLY the tagged bytes — one SHA anchors source, ledger, tarballs, edge catalog, mirror, and\n     9\t# evidence. Leg 1b was added 2026-07-31: leg 1 uploads bytes to R2 but the Worker inlines\n    10\t# registry/index.json at BUILD time, so without a Worker deploy a green train can leave the edge\n    11\t# resolving the previous release (observed on v2026.07.30). The readiness\n    12\t# job (R3, scripts/release-readiness.ts) runs first and any red check — including tag-not-on-main\n    13\t# — stops the train before it touches an external surface.\n    14\t#\n    15\t# STAYS DORMANT UNTIL ARMED: the propagation job runs only when the repo VARIABLE\n    16\t# RELEASE_TRAIN_ARMED is \"true\" (a variable, not a secret, so it can gate a job-level `if:`\n    17\t# directly — no guard-step dance needed). Until the operator sets it, a published release runs\n    18\t# readiness (useful signal) and skips propagation. The mirror + deploy legs additionally keep\n    19\t# their own inert-until-armed guards (MIRROR_PUSH_TOKEN, RAILWAY_TOKEN), so arming the train\n    20\t# without arming those legs still no-ops them green. Leg 1 (registry publish) deliberately does\n    21\t# NOT no-op: with R2 keys unset it fails loud (a silent green \"publish\" would mark a release\n    22\t# done while buyers 404 on the tarballs).\n    23\t#\n    24\t# The retired per-push triggers: publish.yml (dry-run on every main push) and mirror-sync.yml\n    25\t# (snapshot per main push) no longer fire on push — the train is their scheduler now; both keep\n    26\t# workflow_dispatch as the manual lever.\n    27\ton:\n    28\t  release:\n    29\t    types: [published]\n    30\t\n    31\tpermissions:\n    32\t  contents: read\n    33\t\n    34\tconcurrency:\n    35\t  group: release-train\n    36\t  cancel-in-progress: false\n    37\t\n    38\tjobs:\n    39\t  readiness:\n    40\t    runs-on: ${{ vars.CI_RUNNER_LINUX || 'ubuntu-latest' }}\n    41\t    timeout-minutes: 20\n    42\t    permissions:\n    43\t      contents: read\n    44\t      checks: read # readiness check 1 reads the check-runs API on the release SHA\n    45\t      pull-requests: read # `bun run sot` tracker-vs-reality reads PR states via `gh pr view`\n    46\t    steps:\n    47\t      - uses: actions/checkout@3d3c42e5aac5ba805825da76410c181273ba90b1 # v7\n    48\t        with:\n    49\t          fetch-depth: 0\n    50\t      - uses: oven-sh/setup-bun@0c5077e51419868618aeaa5fe8019c62421857d6 # v2.2.0\n    51\t        with:\n    52\t          bun-version: \"1.4.2\"\n    53\t      - run: bun install --frozen-lockfile\n    54\t      - name: release readiness (R3)\n    55\t        env:\n    56\t          GH_TOKEN: ${{ github.token }}\n    57\t          # env-indirect, never inlined in run: — a tag name may legally contain `$();|&`\n    58\t          # (github.sha is hex-safe but rides along for consistency).\n    59\t          RELEASE_TAG: ${{ github.event.release.tag_name }}\n    60\t          RELEASE_SHA: ${{ github.sha }}\n    61\t        run: |\n    62\t          bun scripts/release-readiness.ts \\\n    63\t            --tag \"$RELEASE_TAG\" \\\n    64\t            --sha \"$RELEASE_SHA\"\n    65\t\n    66\t  propagate:\n    67\t    needs: readiness\n    68\t    # Dormant until the operator sets the RELEASE_TRAIN_ARMED repo variable to \"true\" (ADR-0318:\n    69\t    # the train ships dormant; W3 arming is an operator act). Skipped-when-unarmed keeps the\n    70\t    # workflow green.\n    71\t    if: vars.RELEASE_TRAIN_ARMED == 'true'\n    72\t    runs-on: ${{ vars.CI_RUNNER_LINUX || 'ubuntu-latest' }}\n    73\t    timeout-minutes: 90\n    74\t    environment: release # ADR-0327 rider 2 (definition-first; free-plan protection rules can't enforce yet)\n    75\t    permissions:\n    76\t      contents: read\n    77\t      actions: write # dispatch same-repo workflows (publish.yml, deploy-worker.yml, mirror-sync.yml, deploy-railway.yml)\n    78\t    steps:\n    79\t      - uses: actions/checkout@3d3c42e5aac5ba805825da76410c181273ba90b1 # v7\n    80\t      # Dispatch a workflow and block until its run concludes; fail the train on a red leg.\n    81\t      # `gh workflow run` returns no run id, so poll for the newest run created after dispatch\n    82\t      # (concurrency: single-operator repo + per-workflow concurrency groups make this safe).\n    83\t      - name: leg helper\n    84\t        run: |\n    85\t          cat > /tmp/dispatch-and-wait.sh <<'EOF'\n    86\t          #!/usr/bin/env bash\n    87\t          set -euo pipefail\n    88\t          repo=\"$1\"; workflow=\"$2\"; shift 2\n    89\t          before=\"$(date -u '+%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ')\"\n    90\t          gh workflow run \"$workflow\" -R \"$repo\" \"$@\"\n    91\t          run_id=\"\"\n    92\t          for _ in $(seq 1 30); do\n    93\t            sleep 10\n    94\t            run_id=\"$(gh run list -R \"$repo\" --workflow \"$workflow\" --created \">$before\" \\\n    95\t              --limit 1 --json databaseId --jq '.[0].databaseId // empty')\"\n    96\t            [ -n \"$run_id\" ] && break\n    97\t          done\n    98\t          if [ -z \"$run_id\" ]; then echo \"::error::$repo/$workflow: dispatched run never appeared\"; exit 1; fi\n    99\t          echo \"watching $repo/$workflow run $run_id\"\n   100\t          gh run watch \"$run_id\" -R \"$repo\" --exit-status --interval 30\n   101\t          EOF\n   102\t          chmod +x /tmp/dispatch-and-wait.sh\n   103\t      - name: leg 1 — registry publish (verify + upload EXACTLY the tagged bytes, LIVE)\n   104\t        env:\n   105\t          GH_TOKEN: ${{ github.token }}\n   106\t          RELEASE_TAG: ${{ github.event.release.tag_name }} # env-indirect, never inlined in run:\n   107\t        run: |\n   108\t          /tmp/dispatch-and-wait.sh \"${{ github.repository }}\" publish.yml \\\n   109\t            -f dry_run=false -f tag=\"$RELEASE_TAG\"\n   110\t      # Leg 1 uploaded the tarball BYTES; this makes them RESOLVABLE. deploy-entry.ts inlines\n   111\t      # registry/index.json into the Worker bundle at build time, so without this leg the edge keeps\n   112\t      # serving its previously-baked catalog and `bun add @caisson/<pkg>` returns the last release —\n   113\t      # exactly what happened on v2026.07.30, where a fully green train left the site advertising an\n   114\t      # entry point the registry could not resolve. Numbered 1b, not 5, because the order is\n   115\t      # load-bearing: after the bytes exist (leg 1), before the site advertises them (leg 4).\n   116\t      - name: leg 1b — registry Worker deploy (bake the tagged index onto the live edge)\n   117\t        env:\n   118\t          GH_TOKEN: ${{ github.token }}\n   119\t          RELEASE_TAG: ${{ github.event.release.tag_name }} # env-indirect, never inlined in run:\n   120\t        run: |\n   121\t          /tmp/dispatch-and-wait.sh \"${{ github.repository }}\" deploy-worker.yml \\\n   122\t            -f ref=\"$RELEASE_TAG\"\n   123\t      - name: leg 2 — public mirror sync (exported at the release tag)\n   124\t        env:\n   125\t          GH_TOKEN: ${{ github.token }}\n   126\t          RELEASE_TAG: ${{ github.event.release.tag_name }} # env-indirect, never inlined in run:\n   127\t        run: |\n   128\t          /tmp/dispatch-and-wait.sh \"${{ github.repository }}\" mirror-sync.yml \\\n   129\t            -f ref=\"$RELEASE_TAG\"\n   130\t      - name: leg 3 — mirror npm publish (caisson-sh/caisson-oss)\n   131\t        # Pre-launch train rides skip the public npm leg (ADR-0329, amends 0325): MIRROR_PUSH_TOKEN\n   132\t        # stopped being an inert-guard when mirror-sync armed it 2026-07-10, so this leg needs its\n   133\t        # own arming variable. Set RELEASE_NPM_MIRROR_ARMED=true at the ADR-0318 W3 public flip.\n   134\t        if: vars.RELEASE_NPM_MIRROR_ARMED == 'true'\n   135\t        env:\n   136\t          # MIRROR_PUSH_TOKEN is the fine-grained PAT on caisson-sh/caisson-oss (contents +\n   137\t          # actions/workflows rw) — the same credential mirror-sync pushes with.\n   138\t          GH_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.MIRROR_PUSH_TOKEN }}\n   139\t        run: /tmp/dispatch-and-wait.sh caisson-sh/caisson-oss publish.yml -f confirm=publish\n   140\t      - name: leg 4 — site redeploy\n   141\t        env:\n   142\t          GH_TOKEN: ${{ github.token }}\n   143\t          RELEASE_TAG: ${{ github.event.release.tag_name }} # env-indirect, never inlined in run:\n   144\t        # require_armed=true: an unarmed deploy leg must FAIL the train, not skip green. Found\n   145\t        # 2026-07-28 during v2026.07.27.1 — the train reported all legs green while the site kept\n   146\t        # serving the previous image, because RAILWAY_TOKEN is not a repo secret.\n   147\t        #\n   148\t        # ref=$RELEASE_TAG: without it, deploy-railway.yml's resolve-ref falls back to the\n   149\t        # dispatched run's github.sha — main HEAD at dispatch time, not the tag. Any merge to main\n   150\t        # during the multi-leg window would then bake a DIFFERENT registry/index.json into\n   151\t        # license/admin than leg 1b baked into the Worker, and the parity probe would red on a\n   152\t        # train that \"worked\". One SHA anchors every leg only if every leg is told which SHA.\n   153\t        run: |\n   154\t          /tmp/dispatch-and-wait.sh \"${{ github.repository }}\" deploy-railway.yml \\\n   155\t            -f require_armed=true -f ref=\"$RELEASE_TAG\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
