{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'nl -ba knowledge/decisions/ADR-0425-bind-release-audit-to-reviewed-parent.md'","aggregated_output":"     1\t# ADR-0425 — Bind release audit to the reviewed parent\n     2\t\n     3\t- Date: 2026-09-16\n     4\t- Status: Accepted — operator R370 / EST-ASK-328\n     5\t- Scope: R4 audit and release readiness\n     6\t- Supersedes: R359 CR-06 exact final-SHA field inside the tagged audit\n     7\t\n     8\t## Decision\n     9\t\n    10\tThe audit uses schema_version 2 and reviewed_sha equal to the tag candidate single parent.\n    11\tIt retains the exact previous release base, release tag, clean verdict, zero blockers,\n    12\tnon-empty reviewed scope and completed code-review/security identities and timestamps.\n    13\tReadiness derives the parent using rev-parse <tag_sha>^, derives the previous release from\n    14\tthat parent, reads the audit blob from the candidate commit, and independently rejects\n    15\tany successor change outside the exact tag-specific audit and checklist paths. The two\n    16\tpath templates live in one constant. Both artifacts must be regular Git blobs. Merge\n    17\tsuccessors are rejected because the reviewed parent must be unambiguous.\n    18\t\n    19\tReview product candidate A, then commit only its audit (naming A) and release checklist\n    20\tas B. The workflow still passes B, and full required CI still binds B. No product, policy,\n    21\tother audit or arbitrary documentation changes can enter B without a new reviewed parent.\n    22\tThis avoids asking a commit to contain its own hash and does not relax the reviewed-byte\n    23\tboundary. The signed release tag and publication remain separately authorized acts.\n    24\t\n    25\t## Verification\n    26\t\n    27\tScratch repositories construct the real A-to-B lifecycle. Tests accept the two-file\n    28\tattestation successor and reject product bytes, neighboring audit/checklist paths and\n    29\tan audit naming another real commit. Dirty working-tree audit bytes cannot substitute\n    30\tfor B. Named guard mutations and byte-identical restoration are recorded in RUN-NOTES.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
