ng failed\" }, 500);\n950-      }\n951-\n952-      try {\n953:        // Atomically transition approved+card-validated → issued. The UPDATE's WHERE re-checks the\n954-        // gate, so a concurrent revoke between the read above and here fails closed (ConflictError).\n955:        const issued = await withAdminWrite(deps.db, (tx) =>\n956-          recordIssuedEval(tx, {\n957-            evalId,\n958:            licenseId: claims.licenseId,\n959:            licenseToken: token,\n960-            windowEnd,\n961-          }),\n962-        );\n963-        return json({\n964-          token,\n965:          licenseId: claims.licenseId,\n966:          expiry: issued.windowEnd,\n967-        });\n968-      } catch (err) {\n969-        if (err instanceof ConflictError) {\n970-          return json({ error: \"eval not issuable\" }, 409);\n971-        }\n972:        process.stderr.write(\"[service-license] eval issue failed\\n\");\n973:        return json({ error: \"eval issue failed\" }, 500);\n974-      }\n975-    }\n976-\n977:    if (pathname === \"/webhook\") {\n978:      // The Paddle MoR webhook destination (license.caisson.sh/webhook, ADR-0108/0116). A real purchase\n979:      // lands here; this route provisions it. It runs BOTH the credit grant AND the entitlement grant in\n980:      // ONE tenant transaction (apply-billing-event.ts) — the seam the services-hardening audit (#3)\n981-      // flagged as bound to no server.\n982-      if (method !== \"POST\") return text(\"method not allowed\", 405);\n983-\n984:      // Rate-gate FIRST: /webhook is the public grey-origin (`*.up.railway.app`) surface, so an\n985-      // unsigned flood (each costs an HMAC compute) is capped before any verify/DB work.\n986:      const limited = rateLimited(\"webhook\", req, \"open\");\n987-      if (limited !== null) return limited;\n988-\n989:      // Fail closed when the webhook secret is unconfigured: a null provider cannot verify ANY signature,\n990-      // so an unverifiable payload must be rejected, never provisioned (security floor — fail-closed auth).\n991-      if (deps.provider === null) return json({ error: \"unauthorized\" }, 401);\n992-\n993:      const signature = req.headers.get(\"paddle-signature\") ?? \"\";\n994-      // Verify against the RAW request body — a parsed + re-serialized payload would not match Paddle's\n995-      // `ts:rawBody` HMAC. `req.text()` reads the bytes exactly as delivered.\n996-      const rawBody = await req.text();\n997-      let result: BillingWebhookResult;\n998-      try {\n999:        // handleBillingWebhook verifies the Paddle signature (throws AuthnError on a missing/invalid one\n1000:        // BEFORE any DB work) then applies the domain event inside `withTenant`: a one-time\n1001:        // purchase.completed grants its entitlements AND any credits; a subscription invoice.paid grants\n1002:        // the cycle credits AND the plan's entitlements — both in one RLS-scoped transaction (ADR-0071/\n1003-        // 0089/0113). The grant stores are idempotent on their natural keys (payment/invoice id), so a\n1004-        // Paddle retry of the same event_id re-applies as a no-op (ADR-0113) — no separate event-dedupe\n1005-        // table needed.\n1006-        result = await handleBillingWebhook(\n1007-          deps.db,\n1008-          deps.provider,\n1009-          rawBody,\n1010:          signature,\n1011-        );\n1012-      } catch (err) {\n1013-        if (err instanceof AuthnError) {\n1014:          // Missing/invalid signature — fail closed, never provision (no secret or body echoed back).\n1015-          return json({ error: \"unauthorized\" }, 401);\n1016-        }\n1017:        // A grant-time failure (unknown price id → fail-closed throw, or a DB error) MUST return non-2xx\n1018-        // so Paddle RETRIES the delivery — a 2xx here would silently drop a real, paid purchase.\n1019:        process.stderr.write(\"[service-license] webhook processing failed\\n\");\n1020:        return json({ error: \"webhook processing failed\" }, 500);\n1021-      }\n1022:      // ADR-0292 — license first-mint webhook-push. AWAITED here — unlike the Discord/PostHog/email\n1023-      // pushes below, which stay genuinely fire-and-forget — so the purchase-confirmation email\n1024-      // built further down can carry the freshly-minted token in THIS SAME delivery, synchronously,\n1025-      // rather than racing a detached mint against an already-fired email. Still strictly\n1026:      // post-commit: the grant's own `withTenant` transaction already committed inside\n1027-      // `handleBillingWebhook` above; the mint runs its OWN separate transaction(s) via\n1028:      // `issueOrReuseLicense`. NEVER throws (`mintLicensePostCommit` catches everything and logs an\n1029-      // operator ALERT on failure) — awaiting it can only ever add a few DB round trips to the\n1030:      // response, never turn a durable grant into a failed webhook. Mints on a GRANT (new\n1031-      // entitlements) or a RENEWAL (an updates-window extension, which grants nothing but still\n1032-      // needs a fresh signed window) — the same two triggers stage 5 and stage 7 of the\n1033-      // buyer-lifecycle audit named as the P0's root cause.\n1034:      const licenseToken: string | null =\n1035-        result.event !== null &&\n1036-        (result.grantedEntitlements.length > 0 ||\n1037-          result.renewedEntitlements.length > 0)\n1038:          ? await mintLicensePostCommit(deps, result.event.accountId)\n1039-          : null;\n1040-      // Post-commit Discord role push (ADR-0203): DETACHED, fired only after the grant durably\n1041-      // landed, and OUTSIDE the grant's try/catch — a misbehaving notifier (even one throwing\n1042-      // synchronously) must never convert a committed grant into a 500 (which would trigger a\n1043-      // pointless Paddle re-delivery). `notifyDiscordGrant` itself never throws; the guards here\n1044-      // are belt-and-braces for injected doubles. Paddle's 2xx never waits on Discord.\n1045-      if (\n1046-        deps.discordNotify !== null &&\n1047-        result.event !== null &&\n1048-        result.grantedEntitlements.length > 0\n1049-      ) {\n1050-        const push: DiscordGrantPush = {\n1051:          accountId: result.event.accountId,\n1052-          entitlements: result.grantedEntitlements,\n1053-        };\n1054-        try {\n1055-          void deps.discordNotify(push).catch(() => {\n1056-            process.stderr.write(\n1057:              \"[service-license] discord notify rejected (ignored)\\n\",\n1058-            );\n1059-          });\n1060-        } catch {\n1061-          process.stderr.write(\n1062:            \"[service-license] discord notify threw (ignored)\\n\",\n1063-          );\n1064-        }\n1065-      }\n1066-      // Post-commit PostHog purchase capture (ADR-0237 F8): same detached contract as the Discord\n1067-      // push — fired only on a durable grant, never delays or fails Paddle's 2xx. Re-deliveries\n1068-      // short-circuit on the grant claim with an empty grant list, so a purchase captures once.\n1069:      // `amountTotal` narrows the event union to the money-carrying kinds (purchase/invoice).\n1070-      if (\n1071-        deps.posthogCapture !== null &&\n1072-        result.event !== null &&\n1073:        \"amountTotal\" in result.event &&\n1074-        result.grantedEntitlements.length > 0\n1075-      ) {\n1076-        const capture: PurchaseCapture = {\n1077:          accountId: result.event.accountId,\n1078-          entitlements: result.grantedEntitlements,\n1079:          amountTotalMinor: result.event.amountTotal,\n1080-          currency: result.event.currency,\n1081-          sourceEventId: result.event.sourceEventId,\n1082-          skuLines: result.skuLines,\n1083-          // G33: the SAME subscription-cycle-vs-first-purchase computation the sibling email\n1084-          // notice makes, further down.\n1085-          subscriptionCycle:\n1086-           