future KMS adapter timeout) — never an unhandled\n459-    // async rejection.\n460-    return { kind: \"sign_failed\" };\n461-  }\n462-\n463-  // Window-changed RE-MINT (ADR-0251 Decision 3): a stored grant exists but its signed window is\n464-  // stale — replace the stored row's token in place (still exactly one row per (account, major)).\n465-  // Late-loser caveat: a mint that hit the `withDeadline` timeout but keeps running in the\n466-  // background (abandoned, not canceled) can still land HERE late — if two renewals for the SAME\n467-  // account race within seconds, the late one's UPDATE can clobber a newer token with a stale one.\n468-  // Self-heals on the account's next renewal event; only reachable once a slow KMS signer replaces\n469-  // the current instant local Ed25519 signer (which never triggers the deadline in the first place).\n470-  if (existing !== null) {\n471-    await withTenant(deps.db, accountId, (tx) =>\n472-      updateLicenseGrantToken(tx, {\n473-        accountId,\n474-        major,\n475-        licenseId: claims.licenseId,\n476-        tier,\n477-        expiry,\n478-        token,\n479-      }),\n480-    );\n481-    return { kind: \"ok\", token, licenseId: claims.licenseId };\n482-  }\n483-\n484-  // Persist, idempotently: a concurrent /issue for the same (accountId, major) may have minted its\n485-  // OWN token and stored it first — `storeLicenseGrant`'s unique-index ON CONFLICT silently drops\n486-  // the loser's insert. Re-read on a lost race so every caller converges on the SAME stored\n487-  // (winning) token, never two live tokens for one (account, major).\n488-  const stored = await withTenant(deps.db, accountId, (tx) =>\n489-    storeLicenseGrant(tx, {\n490-      accountId,\n491-      major,\n492-      licenseId: claims.licenseId,\n493-      tier,\n494-      expiry,\n495-      token,\n496-    }),\n497-  );\n498-  if (stored) {\n499-    return { kind: \"ok\", token, licenseId: claims.licenseId };\n500-  }\n501-  const win