{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_60","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'nl -ba services/support-bot/src/caisson_support_bot/billing_grant.py'","aggregated_output":"     1\t\"\"\"The bot's inbound HTTP surface: liveness + the authed billing-grant + site-escalate pushes.\n     2\t\n     3\tOne aiohttp application serves the container's single inbound port. ``GET /health`` keeps the\n     4\tADR-0105 liveness contract (unauthenticated, readiness-keyed status). ``POST /billing-grant`` (ADR-0203)\n     5\tis the push target ``services/license`` calls after a purchase grant commits and ``apps/site`` calls\n     6\tafter a buyer links Discord (the backfill). ``POST /escalate`` is the push target ``apps/site``'s\n     7\tAsk-AI widget calls when it cannot answer a question — it files through the SAME ``Escalator`` +\n     8\tLinear Triage sink (ADR-0206) the Discord bot's own escalations use, so a site-originated question a\n     9\thuman needs to see gets the same ticket/Triage-issue treatment a Discord one does. Both POST routes\n    10\tare registered ONLY when their own token is configured — unset means the route 404s and the bot runs\n    11\tunaffected (fail-closed, the config-gating rule every optional surface here follows).\n    12\t\n    13\tSecurity posture (identity/security.md):\n    14\t  • Bearer auth BEFORE any body read; the token is variable-length, so both sides are SHA-256-digested\n    15\t    to fixed 32-byte values and compared with ``hmac.compare_digest`` (the variable-length timing-safe\n    16\t    rule — a raw length-mismatch short-circuit would leak the token length).\n    17\t  • The body is pydantic-``extra=\"forbid\"`` validated (the Zod-``.strict()`` analogue) with bounded\n    18\t    fields; ``client_max_size`` caps the payload before parsing.\n    19\t  • The grant reuses the SAME pure helpers ``/grant-role`` uses (``edition_role_id`` /\n    20\t    ``role_outranks_bot``), so the manual and pushed paths cannot drift. The pushed path has no\n    21\t    invoking moderator — the caller is the platform itself, authenticated by the Bearer — so the\n    22\t    ``member_can_manage_role`` invoker check does not apply; the bot-hierarchy check still does.\n    23\t\n    24\taiohttp is discord.py's own HTTP stack (already pinned in uv.lock) — no new dependency class.\n    25\t\"\"\"\n    26\t\n    27\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n    28\t\n    29\timport hashlib\n    30\timport hmac\n    31\timport os\n    32\timport re\n    33\tfrom dataclasses import dataclass\n    34\tfrom pathlib import Path\n    35\tfrom typing import TYPE_CHECKING, Annotated\n    36\t\n    37\timport discord\n    38\tfrom aiohttp import web\n    39\tfrom discord.ext import commands\n    40\tfrom pydantic import BaseModel, ConfigDict, Field, StringConstraints, ValidationError\n    41\t\n    42\tfrom .bot import linear_issue_tracker\n    43\tfrom .config import Settings\n    44\tfrom .contracts import Brief\n    45\tfrom .escalation import Escalator, IssueTracker, TicketStore\n    46\tfrom .lifecycle import PrivilegedWorkClosed, PrivilegedWorkGate\n    47\tfrom .member_mgmt import (\n    48\t    PRIORITY_SUPPORT_ENTITLEMENT_ID,\n    49\t    edition_role_id,\n    50\t    editions_for_entitlements,\n    51\t    priority_support_role_id,\n    52\t    role_outranks_bot,\n    53\t)\n    54\t\n    55\tif TYPE_CHECKING:  # pragma: no cover - typing only (avoids a real import cycle at module load)\n    56\t    import httpx\n    57\t\n    58\t    # `aiohttp.web.Handler` does NOT exist at runtime (checked against the pinned 3.14.3) — the\n    59\t    # canonical export is `aiohttp.typedefs.Handler`. Under `from __future__ import annotations` a\n    60\t    # wrong name here is a silent no-op rather than an ImportError, so pyright is the only thing\n    61\t    # that catches it; keep this import here rather than inlining a Callable alias.\n    62\t    from aiohttp.typedefs import Handler\n    63\t\n    64\t\n    65\tclass BillingGrantRequest(BaseModel):\n    66\t    \"\"\"POST /billing-grant body — purchased entitlement ids, verbatim from the caller's grant.\"\"\"\n    67\t\n    68\t    model_config = ConfigDict(extra=\"forbid\", frozen=True)\n    69\t\n    70\t    # A Discord snowflake in string form (JSON numbers would lose precision past 2^53).\n    71\t    discord_user_id: str = Field(pattern=r\"^[0-9]{1,32}$\")\n    72\t    # Purchased ids (editions / bundle / module slugs) — bounded like the pricebook's own schema.\n    73\t    entitlements: list[Annotated[str, StringConstraints(min_length=1, max_length=128)]] = Field(\n    74\t        min_length=1, max_length=64\n    75\t    )\n    76\t\n    77\t\n    78\tclass SiteEscalateRequest(BaseModel):\n    79\t    \"\"\"POST /escalate body — a question the site Ask-AI widget could not answer.\n    80\t\n    81\t    Bounds mirror the site's own AskBody (`apps/site/lib/ask-ai/handler.ts`): a question up to 2000\n    82\t    chars, plus a short machine-readable reason the widget already has (its EscalationReason union).\n    83\t    \"\"\"\n    84\t\n    85\t    model_config = ConfigDict(extra=\"forbid\", frozen=True)\n    86\t\n    87\t    question: str = Field(min_length=1, max_length=2000)\n    88\t    reason: str = Field(min_length=1, max_length=64)\n    89\t\n    90\t\n    91\tdef bearer_ok(header: str | None, expected: str) -> bool:\n    92\t    \"\"\"Timing-safe Bearer check (variable-length rule: SHA-256 both sides, then compare_digest).\"\"\"\n    93\t    if not expected or header is None or not header.startswith(\"Bearer \"):\n    94\t        return False\n    95\t    presented = header[len(\"Bearer \") :]\n    96\t    return hmac.compare_digest(\n    97\t        hashlib.sha256(presented.encode()).digest(),\n    98\t        hashlib.sha256(expected.encode()).digest(),\n    99\t    )\n   100\t\n   101\t\n   102\tdef grant_guild(bot: commands.Bot, settings: Settings) -> discord.Guild | None:\n   103\t    \"\"\"The ONE guild billing grants apply to — never \"whichever guild matched first\".\n   104\t\n   105\t    ``guild_id`` set → that guild or nothing. Unset → the bot's sole guild, and ``None`` when the\n   106\t    bot sits in several (ambiguous — the configured role ids belong to exactly one server, so\n   107\t    granting in \"the first guild that knows the user\" could target the wrong server). Fail-closed.\n   108\t    \"\"\"\n   109\t    if settings.guild_id is not None:\n   110\t        return bot.get_guild(settings.guild_id)\n   111\t    if len(bot.guilds) == 1:\n   112\t        return bot.guilds[0]\n   113\t    return None\n   114\t\n   115\t\n   116\tasync def find_member(guild: discord.Guild, user_id: int) -> discord.Member | None:\n   117\t    \"\"\"Resolve a member in the grant guild — cache first, then a single REST fetch.\n   118\t\n   119\t    ``fetch_member`` needs no privileged intent (it is a targeted REST call, unlike bulk member\n   120\t    enumeration). ``None`` means the user is not in the guild — the caller answers 404 so the\n   121\t    push's log shows the miss.\n   122\t    \"\"\"\n   123\t    member = guild.get_member(user_id)\n   124\t    if member is not None:\n   125\t        return member\n   126\t    try:\n   127\t        return await guild.fetch_member(user_id)\n   128\t    except discord.HTTPException:\n   129\t        return None\n   130\t\n   131\t\n   132\t@dataclass(frozen=True)\n   133\tclass _Deps:\n   134\t    bot: commands.Bot\n   135\t    settings: Settings\n   136\t    token: str\n   137\t    escalate_token: str\n   138\t    store: TicketStore | None\n   139\t    issue_tracker: IssueTracker | None\n   140\t    work_gate: PrivilegedWorkGate\n   141\t\n   142\t\n   143\t_DEPS: web.AppKey[_Deps] = web.AppKey(\"caisson_billing_grant_deps\")\n   144\t\n   145\t# The house production-response header floor (identity/security.md, Headers). Byte-identical to the\n   146\t# TypeScript services' own SECURITY_HEADERS consts (services/docs/src/app.ts, services/license/src/\n   147\t# app.ts, packages/mcp-server/src/http.ts) — this service was the only surface in the fleet missing\n   148\t# them (CLOUD-AUDIT F-10: /health answered 200 with none of the three).\n   149\t#\n   150\t# Applied in the app's response path, NOT at the edge, because this origin is reachable directly on\n   151\t# caisson-support-bot-production.up.railway.app — the same shape as the F-03 bypass, where an edge\n   152\t# gate bound a hostname and the Railway origin answered around it.\n   153\tSECURITY_HEADERS: dict[str, str] = {\n   154\t    \"X-Content-Type-Options\": \"nosniff\",\n   155\t    \"X-Frame-Options\": \"DENY\",\n   156\t    \"Strict-Transport-Security\": \"max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains\",\n   157\t}\n   158\t\n   159\t# The serving revision — which commit this container was built from. The Python port of\n   160\t# packages/kernel/src/revision.ts; same carrier file, same strictness, same `unknown` fallback.\n   161\t#\n   162\t# Kept OUT of SECURITY_HEADERS above because that dict carries a documented byte-identity claim\n   163\t# against the three TypeScript SECURITY_HEADERS consts, and quietly adding a fourth key would make\n   164\t# that comment false. The middleware applies the merged dict instead.\n   165\tREVISION_HEADER = \"x-caisson-revision\"\n   166\tUNKNOWN_REVISION = \"unknown\"\n   167\t_COMMIT_SHA = re.compile(r\"^[0-9a-f]{40}$\")\n   168\t\n   169\t\n   170\tdef _read_serving_revision() -> str:\n   171\t    \"\"\"Read the repo-root ``.caisson-revision`` carrier once, at import.\n   172\t\n   173\t    Anything that is not a full 40-char commit sha — the committed ``unknown`` placeholder, a\n   174\t    truncated write, a missing file on a local run — collapses to ``unknown``. A header that\n   175\t    reports a half-written value is worse than one that admits it does not know.\n   176\t\n   177\t    Unlike the three Next services this needs no path override: WORKDIR is ``/app`` and the CMD\n   178\t    does not chdir, so the cwd-relative default already resolves ``/app/.caisson-revision``. The\n   179\t    override is honoured anyway so the two implementations stay behaviourally identical.\n   180\t    \"\"\"\n   181\t    override = os.environ.get(\"CAISSON_REVISION_PATH\", \"\").strip()\n   182\t    path = Path(override) if override else Path.cwd() / \".caisson-revision\"\n   183\t    try:\n   184\t        raw = path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\").strip()\n   185\t    except OSError:\n   186\t        return UNKNOWN_REVISION\n   187\t    return raw if _COMMIT_SHA.fullmatch(raw) else UNKNOWN_REVISION\n   188\t\n   189\t\n   190\t# Resolved once: the answer cannot change for the lifetime of a process, and this is applied to\n   191\t# every response.\n   192\tRESPONSE_HEADERS: dict[str, str] = {\n   193\t    **SECURITY_HEADERS,\n   194\t    REVISION_HEADER: _read_serving_revision(),\n   195\t}\n   196\t\n   197\t\n   198\t@web.middleware\n   199\tasync def _security_headers(request: web.Request, handler: Handler) -> web.StreamResponse:\n   200\t    \"\"\"Set the header floor on every response, including aiohttp's own generated errors.\n   201\t\n   202\t    aiohttp surfaces a router miss (404 — the state both POST routes sit in when their token is\n   203\t    unset), a method mismatch (405), and a ``client_max_size`` overflow (413) by RAISING\n   204\t    ``web.HTTPException`` rather than returning it, so a middleware that only decorates the returned\n   205\t    response would leave exactly the responses an unauthenticated scanner sees bare.\n   206\t    \"\"\"\n   207\t    try:\n   208\t        response = await handler(request)\n   209\t    except web.HTTPException as exc:\n   210\t        exc.headers.update(RESPONSE_HEADERS)\n   211\t        raise\n   212\t    response.headers.update(RESPONSE_HEADERS)\n   213\t    return response\n   214\t\n   215\t\n   216\tasync def _handle_health(request: web.Request) -> web.Response:\n   217\t    deps = request.app[_DEPS]\n   218\t    ready = deps.bot.is_ready()\n   219\t    return web.json_response({\"ok\": ready}, status=200 if ready else 503)\n   220\t\n   221\t\n   222\tasync def _handle_site_escalate(request: web.Request) -> web.Response:\n   223\t    deps = request.app[_DEPS]\n   224\t    # Auth FIRST — before any body read, mirroring /billing-grant's own posture.\n   225\t    if not bearer_ok(request.headers.get(\"Authorization\"), deps.escalate_token):\n   226\t        return web.json_response({\"ok\": False, \"error\": \"unauthorized\"}, status=401)\n   227\t    try:\n   228\t        async with deps.work_gate.track():\n   229\t            try:\n   230\t                payload = SiteEscalateRequest.model_validate_json(await request.read())\n   231\t            except ValidationError:\n   232\t                return web.json_response({\"ok\": False, \"error\": \"invalid body\"}, status=400)\n   233\t\n   234\t            # Reuses the SAME Escalator + Linear Triage sink the Discord bot's own unresolved\n   235\t            # questions file through (ADR-0206) — no second Linear client, no second ticket table.\n   236\t            brief = Brief(\n   237\t                question=payload.question,\n   238\t                summary=f\"Escalated from the site Ask-AI widget (reason: {payload.reason}).\",\n   239\t            )\n   240\t            await Escalator(store=deps.store, issue_tracker=deps.issue_tracker).escalate(brief)\n   241\t            return web.json_response({\"ok\": True})\n   242\t    except PrivilegedWorkClosed:\n   243\t        return web.json_response({\"ok\": False, \"error\": \"shutting down\"}, status=503)\n   244\t\n   245\t\n   246\tasync def _handle_billing_grant(request: web.Request) -> web.Response:\n   247\t    deps = request.app[_DEPS]\n   248\t    # Auth FIRST — before any body read, mirroring the license service's verify-before-parse posture.\n   249\t    if not bearer_ok(request.headers.get(\"Authorization\"), deps.token):\n   250\t        return web.json_response({\"ok\": False, \"error\": \"unauthorized\"}, status=401)\n   251\t    try:\n   252\t        async with deps.work_gate.track():\n   253\t            return await _apply_billing_grant(request, deps)\n   254\t    except PrivilegedWorkClosed:\n   255\t        return web.json_response({\"ok\": False, \"error\": \"shutting down\"}, status=503)\n   256\t\n   257\t\n   258\tasync def _apply_billing_grant(request: web.Request, deps: _Deps) -> web.Response:\n   259\t    \"\"\"Validate and apply one retry-safe grant while the shutdown gate tracks this task.\"\"\"\n   260\t    if not deps.bot.is_ready():\n   261\t        # The gateway is not up yet — the caller's fetch fails visibly and its push is fire-and-forget;\n   262\t        # the site backfill can simply be retried by re-visiting the page.\n   263\t        return web.json_response({\"ok\": False, \"error\": \"bot not ready\"}, status=503)\n   264\t\n   265\t    try:\n   266\t        payload = BillingGrantRequest.model_validate_json(await request.read())\n   267\t    except ValidationError:\n   268\t        # Never echo the rejected body back (redaction-safe, the parseStrict convention).\n   269\t        return web.json_response({\"ok\": False, \"error\": \"invalid body\"}, status=400)\n   270\t\n   271\t    guild = grant_guild(deps.bot, deps.settings)\n   272\t    if guild is None:\n   273\t        # No unambiguous grant target (GUILD_ID unset while the bot sits in several guilds, or the\n   274\t        # bot is not in the configured guild) — refuse rather than guess a server.\n   275\t        return web.json_response({\"ok\": False, \"error\": \"grant guild unresolved\"}, status=503)\n   276\t    member = await find_member(guild, int(payload.discord_user_id))\n   277\t    if member is None:\n   278\t        return web.json_response({\"ok\": False, \"error\": \"member not found\"}, status=404)\n   279\t\n   280\t    # Idempotency is explicit rather than merely relying on Discord add_roles' set-like semantics:\n   281\t    # a retry filters every role the member already holds and becomes a no-op.\n   282\t    existing_role_ids = {role.id for role in member.roles}\n   283\t    roles: list[discord.Role] = []\n   284\t\n   285\t    def add_if_grantable(role: discord.Role | None) -> None:\n   286\t        if (\n   287\t            role is not None\n   288\t            and role.id not in existing_role_ids\n   289\t            and all(candidate.id != role.id for candidate in roles)\n   290\t            and not role_outranks_bot(role, guild.me.top_role)\n   291\t        ):\n   292\t            roles.append(role)\n   293\t\n   294\t    for edition in editions_for_entitlements(list(payload.entitlements)):\n   295\t        role_id = edition_role_id(deps.settings, edition)\n   296\t        add_if_grantable(guild.get_role(role_id) if role_id is not None else None)\n   297\t    # Priority-support (ADR-0278/0288): a standalone id, deliberately outside `editions_for_\n   298\t    # entitlements` (a plain bundle purchase must never grant it). Fail-closed like every other\n   299\t    # role here — an unset role id or an unmanageable role is a benign no-op, never an error.\n   300\t    if PRIORITY_SUPPORT_ENTITLEMENT_ID in payload.entitlements:\n   301\t        role_id = priority_support_role_id(deps.settings)\n   302\t        add_if_grantable(guild.get_role(role_id) if role_id is not None else None)\n   303\t    if deps.settings.customer_role_id is not None:\n   304\t        add_if_grantable(guild.get_role(deps.settings.customer_role_id))\n   305\t    if not roles:\n   306\t        # Nothing configured/manageable for these entitlements — a benign no-op, not an error.\n   307\t        return web.json_response({\"ok\": True, \"granted\": []})\n   308\t\n   309\t    try:\n   310\t        reason = f\"billing-grant: {', '.join(payload.entitlements[:8])}\"[:400]\n   311\t        await member.add_roles(*roles, reason=reason)\n   312\t    except discord.HTTPException:\n   313\t        # A caller retry is safe: already-applied roles are filtered on its next attempt.\n   314\t        return web.json_response({\"ok\": False, \"error\": \"role grant failed\"}, status=502)\n   315\t    return web.json_response({\"ok\": True, \"granted\": [r.name for r in roles]})\n   316\t\n   317\t\n   318\tdef build_app(\n   319\t    *,\n   320\t    bot: commands.Bot,\n   321\t    settings: Settings,\n   322\t    store: TicketStore | None = None,\n   323\t    http_client: httpx.AsyncClient | None = None,\n   324\t    work_gate: PrivilegedWorkGate | None = None,\n   325\t) -> web.Application:\n   326\t    \"\"\"The inbound app: /health always; /billing-grant and /escalate each only when their own token\n   327\t    is configured. ``store``/``http_client`` back /escalate's ticket persistence + Linear sink\n   328\t    (``__main__.py`` passes the SAME instances the Discord bot's own escalations use); omitting them\n   329\t    (as every existing test does) degrades /escalate to \"accepts the push, files nothing durable\" —\n   330\t    never a 500.\n   331\t    \"\"\"\n   332\t    app = web.Application(client_max_size=64 * 1024, middlewares=[_security_headers])\n   333\t    app[_DEPS] = _Deps(\n   334\t        bot=bot,\n   335\t        settings=settings,\n   336\t        token=settings.billing_grant_token or \"\",\n   337\t        escalate_token=settings.site_escalate_token or \"\",\n   338\t        store=store,\n   339\t        issue_tracker=linear_issue_tracker(settings, http_client),\n   340\t        work_gate=work_gate or PrivilegedWorkGate(),\n   341\t    )\n   342\t    app.router.add_get(\"/health\", _handle_health)\n   343\t    if settings.billing_grant_token:\n   344\t        app.router.add_post(\"/billing-grant\", _handle_billing_grant)\n   345\t    if settings.site_escalate_token:\n   346\t        app.router.add_post(\"/escalate\", _handle_site_escalate)\n   347\t    return app\n   348\t\n   349\t\n   350\tasync def serve_http(\n   351\t    *,\n   352\t    bot: commands.Bot,\n   353\t    settings: Settings,\n   354\t    port: int,\n   355\t    store: TicketStore | None = None,\n   356\t    http_client: httpx.AsyncClient | None = None,\n   357\t    work_gate: PrivilegedWorkGate | None = None,\n   358\t    host: str = \"0.0.0.0\",  # noqa: S104 - container inbound bind; the intended surface (was health.py's).\n   359\t) -> web.AppRunner:\n   360\t    \"\"\"Start the inbound HTTP server; the caller owns ``await runner.cleanup()`` on shutdown.\"\"\"\n   361\t    runner = web.AppRunner(\n   362\t        build_app(\n   363\t            bot=bot,\n   364\t            settings=settings,\n   365\t            store=store,\n   366\t            http_client=http_client,\n   367\t            work_gate=work_gate,\n   368\t        )\n   369\t    )\n   370\t    await runner.setup()\n   371\t    site = web.TCPSite(runner, host, port)\n   372\t    await site.start()\n   373\t    return runner\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
