version commit — anchors source, ledger, tarballs, and evidence.\n.github/workflows/publish.yml-10-#\n.github/workflows/publish.yml-11-# ORDERING (structural, not `needs:` — GitHub Actions `needs:` cannot cross workflow files):\n.github/workflows/publish.yml:12:# this workflow only runs via workflow_dispatch (the release train's leg 1, or a manual operator\n.github/workflows/publish.yml-13-# dispatch), and the train's readiness job has already verified ci.yml's required checks green\n.github/workflows/publish.yml:14:# on the release SHA before dispatching. Main-only (ADR-0021); the tag must be an ancestor of\n.github/workflows/publish.yml-15-# origin/main (verified below).\n.github/workflows/publish.yml-16-#\n.github/workflows/publish.yml:17:# Buyer delivery = self-hosted npm registry (registry.caisson.sh, ADR-0223). Auth: R2 writes use\n.github/workflows/publish.yml-18-# S3-compatible scoped R2 access keys (R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID / R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY / R2_ACCOUNT_ID\n.github/workflows/publish.yml-19-# repo secrets, bucket caisson-registry-tarballs). contents:write is GONE — this job pushes\n.github/workflows/publish.yml:20:# nothing anywhere (the old commit-back was the ADR-0325 provenance defect).\n.github/workflows/publish.yml-21-#\n.github/workflows/publish.yml-22-# Everything is guarded by CAISSON_PUBLISH_DRY_RUN (default \"true\"): dry-run verifies the\n.github/workflows/publish.yml:23:# ledger/sidecar/index consistency at the tag and logs the upload plan, writing NOTHING to R2.\n.github/workflows/publish.yml:24:# Dispatch with dry_run=false (the train passes it) for a live publish.\n.github/workflows/publish.yml-25-#\n.github/workflows/publish.yml:26:# P5-25: GHEC provenance attestation = DECLINED. Lightweight provenance is already embedded in\n.github/workflows/publish.yml:27:#        each LedgerEntry's gateAttestation field; a full SLSA/GHEC attestation blob is deferred\n.github/workflows/publish.yml-28-#        (re-raised by the 2026-07-11 Codex audit as a possible rider — still deferred, the\n.github/workflows/publish.yml:29:#        version-PR + tag-anchored flow closes the gap it targeted).\n.github/workflows/publish.yml-30-on:\n.github/workflows/publish.yml:31:  workflow_dispatch:\n.github/workflows/publish.yml-32-    inputs:\n.github/workflows/publish.yml:33:      tag:\n.github/workflows/publish.yml:34:        description: \"The release tag to publish (checked out, verified, and published byte-exact)\"\n.github/workflows/publish.yml-35-        required: true\n.github/workflows/publish.yml:36:      dry_run:\n.github/workflows/publish.yml:37:        description: \"Set to 'false' to run a LIVE publish (verify at the tag + upload missing tarballs to R2)\"\n.github/workflows/publish.yml-38-        required: false\n.github/workflows/publish.yml-39-        default: \"true\"\n.github/workflows/publish.yml-40-\n.github/workflows/publish.yml:41:permissions:\n.github/workflows/publish.yml-42-  contents: read\n.github/workflows/publish.yml-43-\n.github/workflows/publish.yml-44-# cancel-in-progress: false (not true) — an in-flight run uploads tarballs, so it must finish\n.github/workflows/publish.yml-45-# rather than be killed mid-step; a second dispatch queues behind it.\n.github/workflows/publish.yml-46-concurrency:\n.github/workflows/publish.yml:47:  group: publish-and-index\n.github/workflows/publish.yml-48-  cancel-in-progress: false\n.github/workflows/publish.yml-49-\n.github/workflows/publish.yml-50-jobs:\n.github/workflows/publish.yml:51:  publish-and-index:\n.github/workflows/publish.yml-52-    if: github.ref == 'refs/heads/main'\n.github/workflows/publish.yml:53:    # Blacksmith per ADR-0365 (fleet-only sweep; R2 write creds accepted on VM-per-job runners). Write/publish privilege belongs\n.github/workflows/publish.yml-54-    # on a clean hosted runner, not third-party compute (ADR-0326). `aws` CLI is preinstalled.\n.github/workflows/publish.yml-55-    runs-on: ${{ vars.CI_RUNNER_LINUX || 'ubuntu-latest' }}\n.github/wo