{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_66","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'nl -ba .github/workflows/mirror-sync.yml'","aggregated_output":"     1\tname: mirror-sync\n     2\t# Append-syncs the open (Apache-2.0) base into the public mirror repo caisson-sh/caisson-oss.\n     3\t# Runs scripts/export-public-mirror.ts (the exporter — package selection, @caisson-sh/* scope\n     4\t# rename, self-containment gate), then clones the mirror, replaces its working tree with the\n     5\t# fresh export, and pushes ONE new commit (\"chore: mirror sync from <source sha>\") on top.\n     6\t#\n     7\t# APPEND-ONLY MODEL (ADR-0318 F2/F3 — supersedes the original force-push snapshot model): the\n     8\t# mirror's history was backfilled once at the 2026-07-10 cut-over (gate-passing exporter runs at\n     9\t# real historical SHAs, committed at cut-over — NEVER backdated; the real milestone date lives in\n    10\t# the commit message only) and every sync since APPENDS. Never force-push here again — a rewrite\n    11\t# would break clones/stars and violate the append-only lock. Development, blame, and PRs still\n    12\t# live in THIS (private) repo; the mirror remains a generated read-only artifact (see\n    13\t# scripts/mirror-assets/CONTRIBUTING.md).\n    14\t#\n    15\t# STAYS INERT UNTIL ARMED: MIRROR_PUSH_TOKEN (a fine-grained PAT scoped to contents:write on\n    16\t# caisson-sh/caisson-oss ONLY) gates every real step via the guard below — absent token, the job\n    17\t# runs as a GREEN no-op (same posture as deploy-railway.yml).\n    18\t# TRIGGER: the release train (ADR-0318 R1/R2 — release-train.yml dispatches this as leg 2) or a\n    19\t# manual dispatch. The per-main-push trigger is RETIRED (Kickoff M, W4): under the append-only\n    20\t# mirror model a sync per push would mint a mirror commit per merge; the mirror advances per\n    21\t# RELEASE instead.\n    22\ton:\n    23\t  workflow_dispatch:\n    24\t    inputs:\n    25\t      ref:\n    26\t        # ADR-0325: the release train passes the release tag so the mirror export is anchored to\n    27\t        # the SAME SHA as the tarballs/ledger. Empty (a manual dispatch) = default branch tip.\n    28\t        description: \"Tag or SHA to export from (the release train passes the release tag)\"\n    29\t        required: false\n    30\t        default: \"\"\n    31\t\n    32\tpermissions:\n    33\t  contents: read\n    34\t\n    35\tconcurrency:\n    36\t  group: mirror-sync\n    37\t  cancel-in-progress: false\n    38\t\n    39\tjobs:\n    40\t  mirror-sync:\n    41\t    # Blacksmith per ADR-0365 (fleet-only sweep; the cross-repo push token accepted on VM-per-job runners) → a write cred to\n    42\t    # an external repo stays off the fleet, same posture as deploy-railway.yml's RAILWAY_TOKEN.\n    43\t    runs-on: ${{ vars.CI_RUNNER_LINUX || 'ubuntu-latest' }}\n    44\t    # Raised from 20 when the pre-push verification gate landed: the job now installs, builds, tests,\n    45\t    # lints and format-checks the exported artifact on top of exporting it (~10 min locally).\n    46\t    timeout-minutes: 30\n    47\t    environment: release # ADR-0327 rider 2 parity — this job reads MIRROR_PUSH_TOKEN (a release-propagation leg)\n    48\t    steps:\n    49\t      # Inert-until-armed guard (mirrors deploy-railway.yml): `secrets` can't be read in a job/step\n    50\t      # `if:`, so map it to an env here and publish an `armed` output. Absent token → every step\n    51\t      # below skips → the job succeeds as a no-op instead of failing (the mirror repo may not exist\n    52\t      # yet). Does NOT arm the sync itself — it self-arms when the operator sets the secret.\n    53\t      - name: arm check (MIRROR_PUSH_TOKEN present?)\n    54\t        id: guard\n    55\t        env:\n    56\t          MIRROR_PUSH_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.MIRROR_PUSH_TOKEN }}\n    57\t        run: |\n    58\t          if [ -n \"${MIRROR_PUSH_TOKEN}\" ]; then\n    59\t            echo \"armed=true\" >> \"$GITHUB_OUTPUT\"\n    60\t          else\n    61\t            echo \"armed=false\" >> \"$GITHUB_OUTPUT\"\n    62\t            echo \"::notice::mirror-sync is inert — MIRROR_PUSH_TOKEN not set; skipping (mirror repo may not exist yet)\"\n    63\t          fi\n    64\t      - uses: actions/checkout@3d3c42e5aac5ba805825da76410c181273ba90b1 # v7\n    65\t        if: steps.guard.outputs.armed == 'true'\n    66\t        with:\n    67\t          # Empty ref = the checkout action's default (the dispatching branch tip).\n    68\t          ref: ${{ github.event.inputs.ref }}\n    69\t      - uses: oven-sh/setup-bun@0c5077e51419868618aeaa5fe8019c62421857d6 # v2.2.0\n    70\t        if: steps.guard.outputs.armed == 'true'\n    71\t        with:\n    72\t          bun-version: \"1.4.2\"\n    73\t      - name: install\n    74\t        if: steps.guard.outputs.armed == 'true'\n    75\t        run: bun install --frozen-lockfile\n    76\t      - name: export public mirror\n    77\t        if: steps.guard.outputs.armed == 'true'\n    78\t        run: |\n    79\t          bun scripts/export-public-mirror.ts \\\n    80\t            --out mirror-out \\\n    81\t            --generated-at \"$(git log -1 --format=%cs)\"\n    82\t          # Repository-boundary marker for the verify legs below: oxlint/oxfmt discover ignore\n    83\t          # files by walking UP until a repo boundary, and mirror-out sits inside THIS repo whose\n    84\t          # root .gitignore lists it — markerless, both tools match ZERO files (oxlint exit 1,\n    85\t          # oxfmt exit 2). The real public clone has a .git; this makes the gate see what a\n    86\t          # stranger's checkout sees. Stripped with the other verification artifacts before push.\n    87\t          mkdir mirror-out/.git\n    88\t      # PRE-PUSH VERIFICATION GATE. Everything below this comment runs against the EXPORTED\n    89\t      # ARTIFACT, in `mirror-out`, before a single byte reaches the public repo — the mirror's own\n    90\t      # ci.yml (scripts/mirror-assets/ci.yml) runs the same five legs, but only AFTER the push, so\n    91\t      # on its own it can only ever tell us the mirror is already publicly broken. The exporter's\n    92\t      # internal gates (self-containment, entitlement tokens, leakage) prove the SELECTION is\n    93\t      # right; these prove the RESULT actually works standalone under the renamed @caisson-sh/*\n    94\t      # scope. `bun install` here is deliberately NOT --frozen-lockfile: the mirror ships no\n    95\t      # lockfile (it is a generated tree), so this resolves fresh exactly as a stranger cloning\n    96\t      # the public repo would. A failure here fails the job with nothing pushed.\n    97\t      - name: verify export — install\n    98\t        if: steps.guard.outputs.armed == 'true'\n    99\t        working-directory: mirror-out\n   100\t        run: bun install\n   101\t      - name: verify export — typecheck + build\n   102\t        if: steps.guard.outputs.armed == 'true'\n   103\t        working-directory: mirror-out\n   104\t        run: bun run build\n   105\t      - name: verify export — test\n   106\t        if: steps.guard.outputs.armed == 'true'\n   107\t        working-directory: mirror-out\n   108\t        run: bun test\n   109\t      - name: verify export — lint\n   110\t        if: steps.guard.outputs.armed == 'true'\n   111\t        working-directory: mirror-out\n   112\t        run: bun run lint\n   113\t      - name: verify export — format\n   114\t        if: steps.guard.outputs.armed == 'true'\n   115\t        working-directory: mirror-out\n   116\t        run: bun run format:check\n   117\t      # Remove what the five verification steps just built, so the tree copied below is the tree\n   118\t      # the exporter produced and nothing more. The mirror's own shipped .gitignore already lists\n   119\t      # all five of these, so they could not be COMMITTED either way — what this actually prevents\n   120\t      # is `cp -r` duplicating a ~1900-package node_modules across 17 workspaces into the clone on\n   121\t      # every sync. Belt-and-braces on the .gitignore, and cheap.\n   122\t      - name: verify export — strip verification artifacts\n   123\t        if: steps.guard.outputs.armed == 'true'\n   124\t        run: |\n   125\t          set -e\n   126\t          find mirror-out -name node_modules -type d -prune -exec rm -rf {} +\n   127\t          find mirror-out -name dist -type d -prune -exec rm -rf {} +\n   128\t          find mirror-out -name '.turbo' -type d -prune -exec rm -rf {} +\n   129\t          find mirror-out -name '*.tsbuildinfo' -delete\n   130\t          rm -f mirror-out/bun.lock\n   131\t          rm -rf mirror-out/.git\n   132\t      - name: append sync commit to caisson-sh/caisson-oss (never force)\n   133\t        if: steps.guard.outputs.armed == 'true'\n   134\t        env:\n   135\t          MIRROR_PUSH_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.MIRROR_PUSH_TOKEN }}\n   136\t        run: |\n   137\t          set -e\n   138\t          SOURCE_SHA=\"$(git rev-parse --short HEAD)\"\n   139\t          git clone --depth 1 --branch main -q \\\n   140\t            \"https://x-access-token:${MIRROR_PUSH_TOKEN}@github.com/caisson-sh/caisson-oss.git\" mirror-clone\n   141\t          # Replace the clone's working tree with the fresh export; .git stays, so the new\n   142\t          # tree lands as ONE appended commit on the existing history (ADR-0318 append-only).\n   143\t          find mirror-clone -mindepth 1 -maxdepth 1 -not -name .git -exec rm -rf {} +\n   144\t          cp -r mirror-out/. mirror-clone/\n   145\t          cd mirror-clone\n   146\t          git config user.name \"github-actions[bot]\"\n   147\t          git config user.email \"github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com\"\n   148\t          git add -A\n   149\t          if git diff --cached --quiet; then\n   150\t            echo \"mirror already current — nothing to sync\"\n   151\t          else\n   152\t            git commit -q -m \"chore: mirror sync from ${SOURCE_SHA}\"\n   153\t            git push origin HEAD:main\n   154\t          fi\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
