{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_73","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'cat outputs/audit/s8-r370-371-security-brief.md'","aggregated_output":"Tool rules: one command per call; only cat/head/tail/nl/rg/git-read (no sed, no chaining, no redirects); every path relative to this worktree; do not read files outside it; no skill files.\n\ngit: run `git <subcommand> …` directly, never `git -C`, `git -c` or any other option before the subcommand — the working directory is already this worktree; allowed subcommands: blame, describe, diff, diff-tree, log, ls-files, ls-tree, merge-base, name-rev, rev-parse, shortlog, show, status.\n\nS8_REPAIRS_2, R370/R371 renewed security audit. Capability security_audit; role gw-security-auditor; lane deep (canonical gpt-5.6-sol high), concurrency asynchronous but sequential after completed code review, isolation shared-read, permission_profile repo-read. Evidence: complete report with exact base/head, reviewed paths, severity, concrete failure path and unreviewed limits. You are not alone: read only, no edit/revert/delegation/test/package command, external effect, live probe or credential access. Return full report in final response; parent persists it. No skill reads. Any permitted-command denial stops with its verbatim output, no alternatives. Best-effort telemetry HTTP 500 is operator-dispositioned non-blocking. Avoid broad whole-tree searches that can traverse environment files; use named paths.\n\nCandidate HEAD: 23966290343c342d2fcf81775c73d98151223fb1. Subject: three repair commits and outputs/audit/s8-r359-REVIEW.md (two blockers CR-07/08 and warning WR-01). Previous reviewed head c6156d8ce916ced54fba3309b6999c9a7a73167a; intervening 5bd4a97d is receipt-only. Original cumulative context is v2026.08.18..895849a677cdb2e1a9a48d11b9c73a2ac1a0ae6c (89 commits/430 paths), with the original six findings in outputs/audit/s8-r356-retry3-REVIEW.md. The first repair review closed CR-01/02/04/05 at named seams, but not CR-03/06. Check the new remedies and regressions; do not claim a fresh exhaustive cumulative review from a three-repair review. Give PASS / PASS WITH DISCLOSURES / BLOCKED and explicit per-finding closure. A security blocker stops before PR.\n\nOrdered current repairs:\n\n1. a81c537a — CR-07, R370/EST-ASK-328: schema v2 reviewed_sha equals the final candidate's single parent. One constant enumerates exactly the tag-specific audit and checklist paths. Git diff with NUL filenames/no rename detection proves no other changes; committed blobs are read, merge successors and nonregular artifact blobs rejected. Final CI still targets tag SHA. Scratch Git lifecycle accepts reviewed A then attestation-only B; product/neighboring path changes or an audit naming a different real commit fail. ADR-0425.\n2. 18b9c7b7 — CR-08, R371/EST-ASK-329: getCheckoutSession/resolveCheckoutAccount propagate membership errors, reject unverified explicit account selections, and run inside checkout's generic 503 failure boundary. Dashboard getSession fallback unchanged. Production route regression with selected organization and throwing membership resolver proves no entitlement/Paddle call, plus successful org/personal cases and dashboard compatibility. Test doubles are isolated in a child Bun runner. ADR-0426 supersedes only ADR-0424's resolver reuse.\n3. 23966290 — WR-01, S8_REPAIRS_2: reject(approvalId) atomically deletes without spawning, competing with consume. Pending proposals expire after fixed fifteen minutes, timestamp digest-bound; executor rechecks after awaited consume. Memory store reclaims expired capacity on put/reject, refuses expired consumes; durable adapters owe equivalent cleanup/atomicity. Tests include full 1,000-slot rejection/expiry recovery and race orders. ADR-0427 supersedes ADR-0423 no-expiry/consume-only interface. Existing pending tool-exec minor changeset updated; no versions consumed.\n\nCurrent reference packs (full source, use sections as needed):\n- outputs/repomix/2026-09-16-s8-r370-371-approvals.xml — 11 files, 13,827 tokens.\n- outputs/repomix/2026-09-16-s8-r370-371-checkout.xml — 8 files, 7,129 tokens.\n- outputs/repomix/2026-09-16-s8-r370-371-release.xml — 4 files, 12,442 tokens.\nNamed dependencies, ADRs, old repaired paths and tests can also be read directly. These packs cover current source of the three repairs, not the entire cumulative release. Uncommitted audit logs/briefs are parent evidence, not additional product changes.\n\nParent verification, not a request to execute tests: Bun 1.4.2 (744846f84) throughout. CR-07 restored 32 pass/0 fail/70 assertions; three mutation arms red (path restriction, reviewed binding, self-reference). CR-08 isolated actual-route suite 8/0/23; restored cart/auth suite 25/0/78 with accepted pre-existing exit 99; three mutation arms red (fallback, failure boundary, invalid explicit selection); site typecheck/lint pass. WR-01 restored tool/demos/agent-dev suite 46/0/121; five mutation arms red (reject deletion, capacity prune, consume expiry, executor expiry, digest expiry); package build/lint pass. One causal fixture exactOptionalPropertyTypes error was corrected; no product gate bypass. All 11 mutations restored byte-identical hashes, captured in outputs/audit/s8-r370-371-mutations.json and RUN-NOTES.\n\nCombined affected suite: 142 pass/0 fail/500 assertions across 15 files, accepted baseline exit 99. Fresh full root-check equivalent with Turbo --concurrency=2: exit 0, 199/199 tasks, 163 cached, 44.438s; all tail gates ran. Captured suite totals including cache replay: 7,029/0/28,149, deploy tests 64/0/329 and standards 67 checked/5 scaffold-skipped. Logs: outputs/audit/s8-r370-371-targeted.log and s8-r370-371-full-check.log. The child fixture asserts eight passing cases but its internal assertions are not added to the parent's Bun assertion count. Baseline exit-99 evidence remains outputs/audit/s8-r359-baseline-exit99.json, explicitly accepted by operator; do not suppress actual assertion failures.\n\nAuthorization locks the designs above; assess implementation honestly, do not infer success from authorization or tests. Future tag/version/attestation SHA, actual 52-package pack proof, drained changesets, final aggregate SOT and live-hybrid/checklist evidence are later release acts. No placeholder final audit exists. Do not call these pending acts passed or turn their known absence into an unrelated implementation defect. Preserve R344 OS-only image policy and application-CVE disclosures. Original coverage limits and the historic direct bucket-key evidence remain limited, not newly remeasured.\n\nEndpoint: both clean renewed reviews then packet steps 4–6 to one green release PR. No merge, version dispatch, tag, publish, deploy, live probe or branch deletion is authorized.\n\nSecurity scope: assess the three current repairs and the cumulative security-sensitive release seams since v2026.08.18, with exact coverage disclosure. Prior security audits were never dispatched, so there is no inherited security PASS. Prior code reports identify the high-risk paths: packages/local-store/src/embed-scrub-guard.ts, packages/kernel/src/ssrf.ts, services/betterstack-adapter/handler.ts, packages/audit-worm/src/anchor-transparency.ts, apps/site/lib/auth-server.ts, apps/site/lib/auth.ts, apps/site/lib/cart-routes.ts, apps/site/lib/paddle-cart-transaction.ts, apps/site/lib/demos-proxy.ts, packages/kernel/src/origin-gate.ts, apps/admin/src/lib/cloudflare-access.ts, services/license/src/app.ts, services/license/src/deploy.ts, packages/tenancy-rls/src/pool.ts, services/support-bot/src/caisson_support_bot/billing_grant.py, deploy/smoke.ts, deploy/staging-origins.ts, tools/security/image_scan_policy.py, tools/security/rescan_runtime_images.py and release/publish workflows. Prior reports and named files are available; prioritize concrete auth, tenant, credential, money and release-integrity failure paths. Do not label an unexamined cumulative surface audited. The original final R4 audit remains a later tag-bound release artifact.\n\nCompleted renewed code verdict: outputs/audit/s8-r370-371-REVIEW.md, PASS WITH DISCLOSURES, CR-07/08/WR-01 closed. Two warnings need your independent assessment: WR-02 git-show audit bytes pass through trim(), inconsistent with the strict leading frontmatter contract; WR-03 checklist completeness reads the working tree rather than the candidate blob. No product changes have been made after code review. The raw code-review log records a router-level denial at 14:40:40Z for a nonconforming piped rg search, as quoted in its report. It is not a denial of a command satisfying the explicit one-command/no-pipeline rules, and no retry occurred. The operator stop here is a conforming-command denial or review blocker; neither was returned. You must follow the corrected tool rules exactly.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
