{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_74","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'nl -ba knowledge/decisions/ADR-0426-fail-closed-commerce-account-resolution.md'","aggregated_output":"     1\t# ADR-0426 — Fail closed on commerce account resolution\n     2\t\n     3\t- Date: 2026-09-16\n     4\t- Status: Accepted — operator R371 / EST-ASK-329\n     5\t- Scope: site cart checkout identity\n     6\t- Supersedes: ADR-0424 reuse of dashboard getSession for money-path account resolution\n     7\t\n     8\t## Decision\n     9\t\n    10\tCheckout uses getCheckoutSession and resolveCheckoutAccount. The durable Better Auth\n    11\tsession supplies user identity; the same verified membership and personal-bootstrap\n    12\thelpers resolve accounts. Membership errors propagate rather than becoming a personal\n    13\taccount. An explicit account preference must match a verified membership; stale/forged\n    14\tpreferences and empty memberships after bootstrap fail closed. With no preference,\n    15\tnormal verified account selection remains available.\n    16\t\n    17\tThe checkout handler catches session/provider, membership and entitlement failures\n    18\tinside the same error boundary, returns a generic 503 and does not read entitlements\n    19\tor contact Paddle after account-resolution failure. A missing session remains 401.\n    20\tDashboard getSession and its availability fallback are unchanged. No authorization\n    21\tis inferred from the account preference cookie, and no account ID is accepted in the body.\n    22\tAll other ADR-0424 checkout boundaries and disclosed concurrency/SKU limits remain.\n    23\t\n    24\t## Verification\n    25\t\n    26\tThe regression imports the actual production route and actual resolvers with isolated\n    27\tsession/provider, membership, entitlement and Paddle boundary doubles. A selected org\n    28\tplus throwing membership lookup must reach neither entitlements nor transaction creation.\n    29\tCompanion cases preserve dashboard fallback and verify personal/org success, invalid\n    30\tselection, missing session and session-provider errors. The fixture runs in a child\n    31\tBun test process to prevent global module mocks from affecting sibling suites. No live\n    32\tDB, identity-provider or Paddle call is made. Mutations and restoration hashes are\n    33\trecorded in RUN-NOTES.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
